# Sc - Ugur interatomic potential, hard truncation, the reference parameters
#
# pair_style ugur
# pair_coeff * * Sc.ugur Sc
#
# Truncation: hard - phi2 does not vanish at rcut2, it stops at -71.8 meV (2.82 of k_B T at 296 K).  USE for static properties and for lattice dynamics: measured against the measured dispersion the hard sets average 9.7 % over the 33 elements that have one, against 12.6 % for the switched sets, and are closer in 25 of them.  DO NOT use for molecular dynamics: copper, whose step is 8.4 meV, drifts 350 meV/atom/ns in NVE and climbs from 296 K to over 1100 K in 200 ps
# MD: DO NOT USE.  At 600 K the crystal collapses: it reaches 292 K and its potential energy falls below the static lattice.  Static properties from this set are still valid.
#
# Lattice stability: screened on the 8^3 and 9^3 meshes AND along the
# symmetry path; no imaginary modes.
#
# Nudge test: passed - displaced by 1e-5 A and relaxed, the lattice returns.
#
# Fitted to: cohesive energy, lattice constant, bulk modulus and the elastic
# constants of Sc at its experimental lattice constant.  Nothing else.
#
# Format is LAMMPS's Tersoff convention - one line per ordered triple
# (centre, leg, leg) - so that this file and a multi-element one are read the
# same way.  For a single element that is one line.
#
# el1 el2 el3  m D alpha r0 gamma C alpha3 rcut2 rcut3 taper lam2 lam4
Sc Sc Sc 13.219945848895811 0.19619512781935819 0.23477521175680166 3.991067831520803 2.8462936436199359e-06 -0.061579931069994889 0.011738785896708044 8.6059999999999999 4.8825537631448555 -1 0 0
